Subject: [PATCH] AnrController: no "not responding" for an app without a focused window

Ayaneo Pocket DS: with two screens and the controller focus lock, an app can be without a focused
window for a moment: the focus is on the other screen, or an overlay window is being opened. That
is not a hang. The input dispatcher drops the waiting events as soon as the user touches another
app, so the "not responding" dialog (with Wait / Close) is not shown for this case.

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/AnrController.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/AnrController.java
index dba2a1e70..9074cb71f 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/AnrController.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/wm/AnrController.java
@@ -96,6 +96,16 @@ class AnrController {
                     return;
                 }
 
+                // Ayaneo Pocket DS: with two screens and the controller focus lock, an app can be
+                // without a focused window for a moment (the focus is on the other screen, an
+                // overlay is being opened). That is no hang: the input dispatcher drops the events
+                // when the user touches another app. No "not responding" dialog for it.
+                Slog.w(TAG_WM, "No focused window for " + applicationHandle.name
+                        + ": not reported as not responding");
+                if (true) {
+                    return;
+                }
+
                 // App is unresponsive, but we are actively trying to give focus to a window.
                 // Blame the window if possible since the window may not belong to the app.
                 DisplayContent display = mService.mRoot.getDisplayContent(activity.getDisplayId());
